From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sun, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Say what start routine a thread is created with.

Hollow Knight completes Unity's initialisation -- D3D11 through DXVK,
every Mono assembly, PhysX multi-threaded -- and then one thread faults
immediately with c0000005 on execute at address 0: ctxrip=0, every
register zero but rcx/r8/r9, rsp just under a fresh 64 KiB stack. That is
a thread entering a start routine of NULL, not a corrupted call deep in
code.

Two very different causes produce that, and nothing in the log tells them
apart: the guest asked for a NULL start (a function pointer it resolved
came back NULL), or it asked for a real one and this port lost it between
NtCreateThreadEx and the thread's first instruction. Wine traces neither,
so say it once per thread at the creation site. ERR, not TRACE: the
profile's verbose WINEDEBUG turns fixme off and this must survive it.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -1467,6 +1467,9 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtCreateThreadEx( HANDLE *handle, ACCESS_MASK access, OBJECT_ATT
     TEB *teb;
     WOW_TEB *wow_teb;
     unsigned int status;
 
+    /* PW_THREAD_CREATE: a NULL start here means the guest asked for one. */
+    ERR( "PW_THREAD_CREATE start=%p param=%p flags=%#x\n", start, param, (unsigned int)flags );
+
     if (flags & ~supported_flags)
         FIXME( "Unsupported flags %#x.\n", flags );
